07f7","description":"Joseph Bazalgette","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7b01-acb5-8851497db05b","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was the official language of the Holy Roman Empire?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Latin was widely used for the empire\u2019s formal documents and administration, though many languages were spoken across its territories.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-76ce-8ec0-5d5da8f6ba18","description":"Latin","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7063-ac39-2b9c26ebf30e","description":"German","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7cde-8b18-512bfad826f1","description":"Sanskrit","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7b73-a417-ad67b4370171","description":"Greek","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7125-87e5-4e33cc0af078","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which British women\'s organization, founded in 1903 by Emmeline Pankhurst, campaigned militantly for the vote?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Women\'s Social and Political Union adopted the motto \u201cDeeds, not words,\u201d reflecting its use of direct action.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-78c7-9caa-f15fe15b63bb","description":"Women\'s Social and Political Union","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-724a-94ca-87ec0bfb79f4","description":"National Union of Women\'s Suffrage Societies","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7b08-a3f2-3a5307a4a2ca","description":"Women\'s Freedom League","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7cc2-a9a2-62b5ea56b387","description":"Women\'s Land Army","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7c4a-b392-5004993b238f","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What were the Ottoman Empire\u2019s elite slave infantrymen called?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Janissaries formed a standing infantry corps loyal to the sultan. Sipahis, by contrast, were Ottoma