alendar divided into?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Julian calendar had 12 months and used a leap day every fourth year to keep the calendar aligned with the seasons.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7479-9b1f-e16a2fe12d35","description":"12","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-750e-946a-873ff9437407","description":"10","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-763c-b521-d1529821faf2","description":"13","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7878-b92e-359dffc8de9f","description":"11","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7edf-99aa-80187b08c743","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which Russian revolutionary is most associated with the theory of \"permanent revolution\"?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Leon Trotsky argued that Russia\u2019s revolution would have to continue beyond its initial democratic stage and spread internationally.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7a1d-aa35-268ef658eb5a","description":"Leon Trotsky","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7326-9d5f-24fc949abd4a","description":"Vladimir Lenin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7ff2-9c91-3306c31e1f35","description":"Joseph Stalin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7f94-ae55-5a2e5e4bd453","description":"Nikolai Bukharin","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-768c-815b-e39ceea26722","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"With what country did the US almost start a war during the Cuban Missile Crisis?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Soviet Union placed nuclear missiles in Cuba, prompting a confrontation that ended after negotiations between Nikita Khrushchev and John F. Kennedy.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-724e-983a-a03012b383a4","description":"Soviet Union","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7a4f-8d3d-9c65cc3699fa","description":"France","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-714b-8c8d-6d8b02a30bbe","description":"Mexico","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7399-830f-3f904feff9da","description":"Brazil","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7ca1-a9fe-2800e04b602a","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which ancient power defeated Vercingetorix\'s Gallic revolt in 52 BC?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Rome crushed Vercingetorix\'s Gallic revolt at the siege of Alesia in 52 BC under Julius Caesar.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7a39-9434-20d03989131d","description":"Rome","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7571-9e6c-6e1074aea476","description":"Carthage","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7eb1-886c-757e78c1bb6f","description":"Macedon","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-73c1-a868-0ea2fbe7111f","description":"Persia","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7050-a155-e7bbbd4aa1ce","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which of these people was a United States Army general during World War II?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"George S. Patton led the Third Army after the Normandy invasion, and his forces helped liberate much of France.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-79f9-8ec7-2de3f00a8a10","description":"George S. Patton","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7eb4-9624-af1f8b09c355","description":"David Dixon Porter","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-71a7-86fa-d39be9c969a3","description":"George Elliot","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-79e5-8284-9b5e83bb8cd0","description":"Philip Sheridan","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7a0b-8be7-1f9d9b961768","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year did the American Civil War end?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Civil War ended in 1865; Lee\'s surrender at Appomattox Court House in April marked a decisive turning point, though fighting continued briefly elsewhere.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7cbe-8739-f53b493c86e3","description":"1865","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-79d8-a528-e389b2e5a014","description":"1863","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7520-a9ae-c1bc7e8ac873","description":"1861","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7e44-b8a4-d49fef286c65","description":"1877","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-75f9-b8b4-242bff437374","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Betrayed by a fellow gang member, which Wild West outlaw was shot dead in 1882 while dusting a picture frame?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Jesse James was already a notorious post-Civil War outlaw when Robert Ford shot him, hoping to collect a reward.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7b69-aa4b-bdacaaf8c4ec","description":"Jesse James","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7c82-877e-df9e45b53cb2","description":"Billy the Kid","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7c96-bffb-bdb6d6a06151","description":"Butch Cassidy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7c0c-ad1c-9ac16a7e470b","description":"John Wesley Hardin","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-707d-9aff-23c43fa37ec3","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year did the European Union (EU) form?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Maastricht Treaty was signed in 1992 and brought the European Union into existence when it took effect the following year.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7415-aa17-7be9a294ca65","description":"1993","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7e43-8fb0-33dc2b190180","description":"1973","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7590-8419-3bc7ba65232b","description":"1953","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7967-a7e4-a8db54f11c7a","description":"1933","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-721b-a0af-40bc2fa560b5","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"As what is the Frankish ruler Charles the Great better known?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Charlemagne united much of western and central Europe, and his reign helped foster the Carolingian Renaissance.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7af3-b99f-ccfe59bfeb6e","description":"Charlemagne","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7539-a046-8cf78cc65ca8","description":"Charles the Bald","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7802-940a-d19e93ff6e61","description":"Charlione","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7422-9053-975faec64d28","description":"Charity Charles","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7d29-8805-c339e744f531","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What explorer landed in China and reached Kublai Khan\'s court in 1275?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Marco Polo\'s travels, reaching Kublai Khan\'s court around 1275, were recorded in The Travels of Marco Polo.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7606-8c4d-611df78f4970","description":"Marco Polo","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7fb6-a2bf-5c9e79f97186","description":"Christopher Columbus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-723e-a71d-efd4de17b9ec","description":"Ferdinand Magellan","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7538-bc4b-c4a79db8cca5","description":"Francis Drake","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-708f-b779-505e79f2c035","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"When was the first black US President elected?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Barack Obama won the 2008 election and took office in January 2009.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7deb-9f60-458ec19b9b34","description":"2008","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7f1a-a546-0aa2bb3aeac4","description":"2000","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-73ae-8932-6204b5453c8f","description":"2004","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7741-ba81-a50287fe7ed7","description":"2012","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01