iption":"Moscow","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7dd7-adfc-06a95298bd89","description":"Stalingrad","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-76d7-b6b7-1d291d9f4969","description":"Kiev","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-72f5-9956-2a793c5c4026","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year did Napoleon Bonaparte become Emperor of the French?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"In 1804, Napoleon crowned himself Emperor at Notre-Dame, establishing the First French Empire.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7a36-9370-73fb9985ecc0","description":"1804","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7c2c-b3f3-11ca87d9245e","description":"1789","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7121-a9fd-2341e8c9b31a","description":"1799","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7d9a-bd71-67d760e8172a","description":"1815","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7eb4-99a4-d0e7e3eb369a","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who shot Abraham Lincoln?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"John Wilkes Booth shot Lincoln at Ford\u2019s Theatre during a performance of Our American Cousin in 1865.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-78da-8d94-d6707fc5f30f","description":"John Wilkes Booth","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7d59-bbe6-ac65574f9493","description":"Lee Harvey Oswald","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7c8f-a0b9-759286335c53","description":"Mark David Chapman","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7551-a2e1-3c9c0b0a4da8","description":"Leon Czolgosz","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-76e5-a1bc-91a06c174465","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which engineer designed the iron skeleton inside the Statue of Liberty?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Gustave Eiffel engineered the statue\u2019s internal support structure, while sculptor Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Auguste Bartholdi designed its exterior.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7398-a44f-a1310b832795","description":"Gustave Eiffel","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7cb2-a71b-8c3bd0038eeb","description":"Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Auguste Bartholdi","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7121-aa13-5078410d7474","description":"Isambard Kingdom Brunel","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-72a0-b48d-c67f3776e874","description":"Thomas Edison","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7cfd-9fea-2132b0ae09b6","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What epoch questioned the absolute power of royal rulers?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Age of Enlightenment emphasized reason and individual rights. Thinkers such as Montesquieu criticized concentrated power and influenced later constitutional government.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7b8a-be1d-1b878455ba60","description":"Age of Enlightenment","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-78b7-9009-693acf0bf926","description":"Bronze Age","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-71c6-b80d-62100c5cd4fa","description":"Dark Age","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-731a-b4d2-f2fccb35b6c9","description":"Stone Age","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-790b-882b-60b1cd6c3663","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which ancient Chinese site was uncovered by farmers digging a well in 1974?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Terracotta Army consists of thousands of life-size figures buried to accompany Qin Shi Huang in the afterlife.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-710e-b0fa-bf809ea0d7e1","description":"The Terracotta Army","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7a8d-8809-524b545c998b","description":"The Summer Palace","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-758e-93eb-eaf376069ec0","description":"The Temple of Heaven","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7e61-8787-35954c03193b","description":"The Ming Tombs","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-78cb-a591-688aae075a9b","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which Soviet leader denounced Stalin\'s crimes in a famous 1956 \'secret speech\'?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Nikita Khrushchev delivered the speech at a closed session of the Communist Party\'s 20th Congress, helping launch the process of de-Stalinization.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-791a-9db7-143ea196149c","description":"Nikita Khrushchev","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7271-ac82-b891c88881e4","description":"Leonid Brezhnev","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7e23-9b5a-97a5aa010085","description":"Mikhail Gorbachev","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7ac8-bde7-7c731905cd64","description":"Georgy Malenkov","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7c35-b45b-23ae7eb91f67","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was the Prime Minister of The United Kingdom throughout the eighties?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Margaret Thatcher was Prime Minister from 1979 to 1990, covering the whole of the 1980s.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7d82-b692-150885d16a85","description":"Margaret Thatcher","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7ec6-bcdb-cf373e729972","description":"Harold Wilson","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7012-94ba-dd75b8915e95","description":"Tony Blair","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7f93-acea-f6131da5fb6a","description":"John Major","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7b2c-b2dd-bd322921a147","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which US election year were the supporters of the Democratic candidate paraphrasing the popular song \"Hello Dolly\" to \"Hello Lyndon\"?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"In 1964, Lyndon B. Johnson won a full term after succeeding Kennedy, defeating Republican Barry Goldwater in a landslide.","alte