ategory":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"The eldest sons of the kings of which country held the title \'Dauphin\'?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The title came from the Dauphin\u00e9, a region that became part of the royal domain; it was later used for the heir to the French throne.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-785d-8897-b109a118b134","description":"France","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-775e-8a4e-81653c7ee248","description":"Spain","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7a33-bd9a-93c144bea611","description":"Russia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-77e3-beae-31b41d21bec9","description":"Italy","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7688-bab3-c45c323f0e80","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Founded in 1636, what is the oldest university in the USA?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Harvard was named for John Harvard, a clergyman whose bequest of books and money helped the young college grow.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7955-851b-c97680e14e84","description":"Harvard","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7e89-abf8-a48acaefc407","description":"Stanford","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7cd1-87c5-9a54b3244cfd","description":"Cornell","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-74a5-890c-ec41d4ed9f32","description":"UCLA","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-71fb-9d17-faa22b88b448","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In the 1930s, the Soviet Union held a series of notorious staged legal proceedings in which defendants were forced to confess to fabricated crimes. What are these proceedings commonly called?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Show trials targeted figures such as Zinoviev, Kamenev, and Bukharin; their coerced confessions helped Stalin portray political rivals as conspirators.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7dae-8a7d-3ae09fb6c904","description":"Show trials","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-73f6-851d-e5d73676ff37","description":"Witch hunts","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-718a-bfed-07079094e2b9","description":"Military tribunals","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7e80-a711-f93eb20fa315","description":"Truth commissions","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-70de-9596-1742b1f2177a","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who sailed to the new world in The Mayflower?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Pilgrims founded Plymouth Colony in what is now Massachusetts after crossing the Atlantic in 1620.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-78d3-bba3-af8c2ff5e5ac","description":"Pilgrims","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7005-b20c-84f466e0b593","description":"Conquistadors","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7222-8107-3c293fef187f","description":"Explorers","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7f91-acc7-5909b0d5e580","description":"Traders","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7a19-8105-3d763b5ff197","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What is the name of the ancient stone tablet that was carved in 196 B.C., and helped scholars decipher Egyptian hieroglyphs?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Rosetta Stone\'s parallel Greek text gave scholars a way to compare the scripts and decipher Egyptian hieroglyphs.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-780d-90e4-9a2f4cfbd418","description":"The Rosetta Stone","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-784c-b74d-c936275ce897","description":"The Philosopher\'s Stone","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-78fd-af91-684e902a1e64","description":"The Stone of Destiny","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7c10-a1cc-2f36939599d4","description":"The Cornerstone","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-712e-a0e8-38ba12ebbe6b","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which British general commanded the army that surrendered at Yorktown in the American Revolution?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"American and French forces surrounded Charles Cornwallis at Yorktown, while the French navy blocked British relief, forcing his surrender.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7a88-b39b-1bf08df1a5c8","description":"Charles Cornwallis","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7ef4-b726-3fa0e0a0271f","description":"John Burgoyne","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-75d7-b7c8-c8c34ccd3ba2","description":"William Howe","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-754c-a382-d01e8bb1abbc","description":"Henry Clinton","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-752d-93ba-8f39da1493fd","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which Chinese emperor was buried with an army of thousands of life-sized clay soldiers?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Qin Shi Huang unified China and founded the Qin dynasty. His burial complex includes the terracotta army, intended to guard him in the afterlife.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7a69-a55c-900750ff78b4","description":"Qin Shi Huang","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7106-a215-d53af280aa02","description":"Han Wudi","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-77fe-8c28-e11ebb963a16","description":"Kangxi","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-730f-886c-be96bd9aca78","description":"Yongle","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7b22-9ff6-044851a353d8","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Battles known as Con Thien and Hamburger Hill were fought during which 20th century conflict?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Vietnam refers to the Vietnam War, in which the United States fought alongside South Vietnam against North Vietnam and its allies.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7a20-b675-75b1a7b45642","description":"Vietnam","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7fe4-b3fa-e1ed098f1c3f","description":"Iraq","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7981-92e5-6e365d3e1cf9","description":"Korea","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7fc5-99e3-fb2f0550d6b9","description":"Afghanistan","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-79be-857b-8eaae9c025ad","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year did Neil Armstrong first step onto the Moon?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Armstrong stepped onto the lunar surface after the Apollo 11 spacecraft Eagle landed; Buzz Aldrin followed him.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-72bd-80a8-ff15eaff944b","description":"1969","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-75b6-8ef2-c3923664c81f","description":"1967","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-707d-992e-5d17fe32e26b","description":"1971","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-732a-bf88-956d43107ddd","description":"1973","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7e5e-b89b-d96ee3562722","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year was Hong Kong Island formally ceded to Britain under the Treaty of Nanking?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Britain occupied the island in 1841, and it was ceded by the Treaty of Nanking signed in 1842 after the First Opium War.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7a15-b70b-aafdc652c074","description":"1842","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7f08-9895-6c5d66c64ae8","description":"1815","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7876-88de-39a4a6d2d12d","description":"1875","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7637-bb06-6d20a55157ac","description":"1912","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7dec-92ec-9228df27c0f2","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In the Christmas song \'Have Yourself A Merry Little Christmas\' what \"will be out of sight\"?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Troubles are what the lyric says will be out of sight. Hugh Martin wrote the song for the 1944 film musical Meet Me in St. Louis.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7682-937d-153c39e01233","description":"Troubles","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7e83-9f45-b5fa4241b4c1","description":"Difficulties","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7712-833f-4c4a8174b630","description":"Woes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-73f1-9584-ea72e5fd9d03","description":"Sorrows","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-737f-951e-241c8f0f851c","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was the nationality of Rasputin?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Rasputin was born in Siberia, then part of the Russian Empire, and became a confidant of Tsar Nicholas II\'s family.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7532-8552-801483fd8cd4","description":"Russian","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7681-8078-4a32b1cabe56","description":"Indian","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-75be-af53-5f9fe7c948aa","description":"French","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7dac-a31d-ed5ca80552de","description":"Egyptian","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7f8c-acbf-a939a78fb846","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which ancient city\'s most famous facade is carved into a cliff and known as the Treasury?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Petra\u2019s Treasury was likely built as a royal tomb; its name comes from a legend that treasure was hidden in the urn above its entrance.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7705-8043-4fff5b46e2c2","description":"Petra","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-71b5-930b-0a1f33c38246","description":"Palmyra","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7b8a-957a-2831c01d9550","description":"Persepolis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-758e-b435-302aa616fbfb","description":"Ephesus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7001-bb49-dc4cdb55083b","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What country was ruled by Pol Pot, leader of the Khmer Rouge party?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"During Khmer Rouge rule, Cambodia was officially known as Democratic Kampuchea; Vietnam\'s 1979 invasion toppled the regime.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7f63-a1f4-fd6dfacf2c85","description":"Cambodia","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7c64-82e7-63dfa60ef4ac","description":"Ethiopia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7d22-9b42-e34340c79a56","description":"Cuba","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7135-af9e-d6754e51b105","description":"Indonesia","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7bb1-b99c-9a40744114a3","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What name was given to the French government that collaborated with Nazi Germany?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Vichy France was led by Philippe P\u00e9tain after France\'s 1940 armistice with Germany; Charles de Gaulle led the resistance movement from abroad.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7fca-8e7d-da37279fc59e","description":"Vichy France","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-76f8-b494-9a38d99d8a46","description":"Free France","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-76e1-b660-4e53e8a59d48","description":"The Third Republic","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-79f6-b70e-372e2400bba9","description":"The Directory","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7a46-aa33-884fc985a0b2","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What fabled city was German adventurer Philipp Von Hutten searching for when he explored South America in the 1540s?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"El Dorado began as a legend about a gold-covered ruler; over time, the story grew into a fabled city or kingdom of riches.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7ae1-8955-0bbf12e04718","description":"El Dorado","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7b31-92b4-401ffbb8b662","description":"Atlantis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7358-87a9-7549d40c25b6","description":"Shangri-La","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-771b-bb8f-85b84130d300","description":"Camelot","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7bee-9d40-8c757150ffdb","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What came to an end in the United States in December 1933?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The 21st Amendment repealed the 18th Amendment, ending Prohibition. It remains the only constitutional amendment to repeal another.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-73f4-973d-e46700e3e96a","description":"Prohibition","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-784b-8ed4-7824be96c385","description":"Segregation","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7ded-b9a5-da5e54a9ebe6","description":"Slavery","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7243-b37b-c4fd44f0b7d0","description":"British Rule","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-723d-8b6f-4647dcffe581","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which English queen was known as \'The Virgin Queen\'?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Elizabeth I never married, and her reign is often called the Elizabethan era, known for the flourishing of English theater and exploration.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7680-8c60-0a6cadfbfe20","description":"Elizabeth I","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7f24-af53-06b97aeea85a","description":"Mary I","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7075-85d0-37e3eb5e12ea","description":"Anne Boleyn","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-74d0-a7c4-c665599418f9","description":"Victoria","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-78be-90cc-8c971675eb83","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What Russian city was known as Leningrad between 1924 and 1991?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"St Petersburg was renamed Petrograd in 1914 and Leningrad in 1924; the city restored its original name in 1991.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-746c-9f19-3cdbf13b6357","description":"St Petersburg","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7a42-8667-8206046cfdea","description":"Kazan","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7a3f-9cab-1ceb3d00f2bf","description":"Nizhny Novgorod","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7382-8e0e-e75f89943825","description":"Moscow","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-759a-a17b-8a0c0dcd9532","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What ancient civilization occupied the city of Cusco?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Inca made Cusco the capital of their empire, which extended across much of the Andes.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-706f-8d7a-9be61bafb3d5","description":"The Inca","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7652-8915-97394eef152f","description":"The Aztecs","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-75d4-9e05-bd3569009b5b","description":"The Mayans","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-791c-acbc-b1a02dd369b8","description":"The Zapotecs","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-74ca-ab38-dca1e83949ab","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What were the first names of US presidents Madison, Monroe, Polk, and Garfield?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"James Madison and James Monroe served as consecutive presidents, with Monroe following Madison.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7de7-9f94-86a74d3f73d2","description":"James","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7ce8-a2ed-0d353879cc1b","description":"Marshall","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-744f-a1b7-a64b799b9a7b","description":"Theodore","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-71f7-a700-171ab786ea52","description":"Thomas","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5522-7a93-9df7-0444cbfa2257","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f