ountries was founded during the 18th century?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The United States adopted the Declaration of Independence in 1776, and its Constitution took effect in 1789.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7f6c-b77c-8904af1d8b53","description":"The United States of America","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7d7a-8200-157b9c3d85b7","description":"Canada","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7831-8207-65c560f46868","description":"Australia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-730f-b1bd-9c561f74d927","description":"India","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-79ad-b828-76914d6a766d","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was Byzantium renamed in AD 330?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Constantinople was named for Emperor Constantine the Great and became the eastern Roman Empire\u2019s capital.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5523-725f-97ce-663f3a02aa9e","description":"Constantinople","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7d8c-8dc5-9239c40e2e44","description":"Antioch","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7c16-ace1-72ea4d2728c3","description":"Nicaea","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-75f9-bd27-0aa681b2cd15","description":"Alexandria","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7d5e-9efa-0e4742230362","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What man-made waterway did the 1979 Israel-Egypt Peace Treaty allow Israel access to?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Suez Canal is a major shipping route between Europe and Asia, avoiding the much longer trip around Africa.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5523-72c8-a4e0-0beef6692373","description":"The Suez Canal","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7e9a-81f6-ce22927f88dd","description":"The Panama Canal","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7be8-96dd-445a808cb4cd","description":"The Kiel Canal","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7114-9ab5-