nce of the Russian imperial family.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5523-79b7-b488-a3b7b25672ef","description":"Yalta","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7db5-9083-86b66cce75d9","description":"Dresden","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-71aa-8e5f-604b949c61f1","description":"Maastricht","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7511-831f-2c6596cf8000","description":"Versailles","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7c47-8131-133e0b181b2c","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What is the Roman numeral for fifty?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"L represents 50; XL is 40 and LX is 60, using subtraction and addition around it.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7e90-9859-8142d0f3945f","description":"L","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7d96-b2ed-86abdebb1f9e","description":"R","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7e1e-b232-005100fe487f","description":"H","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-777a-bbce-bb4557e31ffb","description":"J","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7db5-ba1d-3f3b7a9de7bd","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What type of people were obsessed with turning ordinary metals into gold in the Middle Ages?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Alchemists pursued the philosopher\u2019s stone, and some also believed it could help create an elixir of life.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7610-9456-75845f018595","description":"Alchemists","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-72f4-8cf8-0a12c07d2a7c","description":"Hussars","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7931-8430-5d68f8def29e","description":"Chandlers","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-79a2-af3d-06e3249380b0","description":"Smelters","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-741d-a03c-5489af74b4cd","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which Chinese dynasty sent the envoy Zhang Qian west to Central Asia around 138 BC?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Han dynasty sent Zhang Qian during Emperor Wu\u2019s reign. His reports and contacts helped spur trade along routes later known as the Silk Road.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7d53-b01f-ea10020ecb1f","description":"Han dynasty","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7ecc-8d79-c4a609e1db6b","description":"Tang dynasty","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-739a-81ed-a79e0135de5a","description":"Ming dynasty","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7727-8100-b8e210ab05fe","description":"Qin dynasty","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7cd5-b618-0a5785f6c13c","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What Shakespearean king was actually king of Scotland for 17 years?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Macbeth ruled from 1040 until his death in 1057; Shakespeare\u2019s play took liberties with the historical king\u2019s story.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5523-72f3-9a35-f3bfe416f20a","description":"Macbeth","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7dba-a3ac-02d98305e479","description":"Lear","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7760-8347-ebfc39d4c633","description":"Hamlet","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7a1b-a569-78012a539abd","description":"Richard III","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-73fd-bf2b-a03eca14be54","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"How many colonies signed the American Declaration of Independence?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Thirteen colonies signed the Declaration; they later became the original states of the United States.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7d61-8ec0-f5915430556a","description":"13","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-78ac-a9ba-33cb69df2452","description":"9","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7afb-af6c-8332e0032d2b","description":"15","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-713e-92a6-cd1