9-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"King Ancus Marcius is said to have built the Sublician Bridge, the first bridge across which river in the 7th century B.C.?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Tiber runs through Rome, and the Sublician Bridge became famous in Roman legend for Horatius Cocles\'s stand against an invading army.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7a8d-86bf-479f9b89f9fe","description":"The Tiber","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7d08-be1c-c639ae851b4c","description":"The Nile","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-71c6-8652-03fd3360726d","description":"The Thames","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-730b-a7d7-6a9c88c0fa6a","description":"The Seine","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-75b1-9a94-e2c1f09ad06b","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What year did World War II begin?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"1939 is the year Germany invaded Poland on September 1; Britain and France declared war two days later.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7369-a75a-28e1f2ed1c99","description":"1939","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7c65-a774-d90a21ab66c2","description":"1941","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7dba-8444-bc4eeada3020","description":"1945","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7b9d-9ede-0c6a26a5b054","description":"1937","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7e40-a8a8-905e34e9f664","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which World War I battle is remembered for the Parisian taxicabs that ferried French troops to the front line in 1914?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The French victory at the Marne halted the German advance toward Paris and helped set the Western Front into a prolonged stalemate.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5523-76d7-a8ce-adc1231f07bd","description":"Battle of the Marne","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7206-b7ef-fa9e6bae6bda","description":"Battle of the Somme","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7bb1-a262-8590066e10d2","description":"Battle of Ypres","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7593-be41-012f2c664315","description":"Battle of Verdun","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7ae1-9f34-07440ddf0748","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was the major economic revolution that started in the 18th century?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Industrial Revolution began in Britain and reshaped manufacturing as production shifted toward machinery and factories.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7d7d-9cd5-ecf845f4d911","description":"The Industrial Revolution","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7fef-9411-f5fa5b03adc0","description":"The French Revolution","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-73f3-81dc-32b88a23dd6b","description":"The American Revolution","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7809-bcaa-d7b883d62b12","description":"The Enlightenment","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7491-b4c7-9db10d7e7221","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What group of ships, commanded by the Duke of Medina, was considered invincible but was defeated by The Royal Navy in 1588?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Spanish Armada was disrupted by English fireships, and storms battered many ships as they retreated around Scotland and Ireland.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7006-b17f-16e0d2e6a4b9","description":"Spanish Armada","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-78f6-aebc-9b40b673cf18","description":"The Napoleonic Fleet","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-73a8-987b-7c2a2403bdfe","description":"The Viking Fleet","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7c5b-9a63-03fd00c4ca7c","description":"The Scottish Armada","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7a9a-8c6e-e5768ebe54c7","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","questi