cription":"Babel","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7731-b299-5b7c13e46fab","description":"Dresden","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7508-95f0-9081413b4df2","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What age preceded the Iron Age?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Bronze is an alloy of copper and tin, and its widespread use gave this period its name.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5523-73e0-8a91-b5ff46d7c81a","description":"The Bronze Age","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-73eb-b8c8-31103ef28148","description":"The Stone Age","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7eae-a668-d09620d4b0da","description":"The Steel Age","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7040-abe3-ad503b7352cd","description":"The Wooden Age","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-78fa-b4d0-795fb786128d","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What notorious event occurred on the 24th October 1929?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Wall Street Crash began with Black Thursday, as investors rushed to sell shares. The market turmoil helped usher in the Great Depression.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7766-b8a7-07f6bcff3404","description":"The Wall Street Crash","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-71b7-9b40-91fd02f16382","description":"The Hindenberg Disaster","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7bd5-ad1f-67a2a01c9fd7","description":"The Assassination of John F. Kennedy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7d06-8643-df1cee9cfece","description":"The Nazi Invasion of Poland","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-75e8-b1b8-6f964cd39445","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In 1945, which German city hosted the trials where former Nazi leaders were prosecuted for war crimes?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The proceedings became known as the Nuremberg Trials and helped establish that political and military leaders could be held individually responsible for international crimes.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7860-af02-8cac706edea5","description":"Nuremberg","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-73b9-81f8-1b7b41a5e0c0","description":"Berlin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7b50-95f7-e8a0f05d5903","description":"Munich","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7f39-a105-e67ef52a78e2","description":"Frankfurt","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7b52-a2cd-be3eb34fe979","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was the term used for a pirate who was licensed by the crown to capture enemy ships and cargo?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A privateer operated under a letter of marque, making attacks on enemy vessels lawful for the crown; pirates acted without that authorization.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7634-a6b6-131cdb47f4d9","description":"A privateer","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-73cc-9517-54e706814695","description":"A smuggler","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-712f-bb12-7cc8c8bb39c4","description":"A mutineer","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7fe3-bcc5-6756a907d492","description":"A sea wolf","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7bf4-b023-24985f662895","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which American gangster was shot dead outside a Chicago cinema in July 1934?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"John Dillinger was shot by FBI agents outside Chicago\'s Biograph Theater on 22 July 1934.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5523-783e-a28c-72dfd9d2437e","description":"John Dillinger","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7fd9-9a4d-52724ba0c3dc","description":"Al Capone","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7e0f-a33f-97aab243c4b1","description":"Vito Corleone","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5523-7549-94c7-060a4155cf59","description":"Ronald Kray","correct_answer":f